{"kind":"report","text":"ceaa2cf1 is answered: discard, and the reason is that the work already shipped.\n\nBoth ideas in the 235-line delta are on main. Commit 08b7c72c, \"Share repeated strings in resident folds\", landed 2026-08-20, one day after adda28c8 which was the delta's base. Main carries intern and internBody over the f.strings pool, decode taking that pool, and pooledStatePayload with pooledJSONText - whose UnmarshalJSON is the same logic as the delta's pooledString: detect an unescaped payload, adopt the bytes between the quotes through the pool, fall back to a normal unmarshal on an escape. The checkpoint half shipped as well; appendBorrowedChunk is at internal/kernel/checkpoint.go:131. Main is also broader: internBody interns Ratify and Supersede targets, which the delta's decode path never touches.\n\nNothing is lost. The delta is preserved as commit 45f40a89 on request/resident-memory-500k. That branch is already an ancestor of main, so the commit lands nothing and adds no code to any artifact; it exists only so the earlier draft is readable without living in a working tree.\n\nI got this wrong once first and the correction is on the record at 7d14feb3, with the assert that recommended landing it retired at 29855f53. I measured the delta against its own base, found -13% memory, and recommended review without asking whether the idea had already shipped. Benchmarking current main shows main is itself 5.6% to 9.2% better than that base on the same benchmarks, so most of what I reported as the delta's win the repository had already captured. I found the duplication only by attempting the carry: git apply --3way conflicted in all three files, and the largest conflict was main's internBody against the delta's decode - two implementations of one idea in one place. A clean apply would have carried duplicate work into a review request.\n\nI am not claiming any residual gain remains. It is tempting to compare main at 135.7M against the delta tree at 129.9M and infer 4.3% more available, and that inference is not supported: those are different codebases at different bases, with the bounded projection transport and the live-membership guard among the differences. If anyone thinks decoding straight into the pool still buys something for the kinds main handles via internBody, that is a fresh measurement against current main under its own request.\n\nYour judgement on this was right throughout: the delta was genuinely at risk, diffing the tree instead of the ref was the right instinct, and declining to commit another actor's unreviewed work was correct. Neither of us checked the cheapest thing, which was whether main had grown the same feature in the meantime.\n\nThe worktree can now be removed safely, since the branch holds the content. I have left it in place rather than delete it on my own judgement, given that removing it was the action you stopped yourself from taking; say the word and it goes."}